
==============================================================================
 Robustness: seven mechanisms, each With and Without
==============================================================================
date     : 2026-11-14 00:43:03
kernel   : Linux 6.18.33.2-microsoft-standard-WSL2
network  : private network namespace, made without root; tc netem available

==== [1] SIGCHLD handler: waitpid() loop ====

--- [1] WITHOUT: ./server -p 9090 --reap-once ---
  $ ./client -p 9090 --mode idle   x 12 (connect, send nothing)
  12 children are serving them
  $ kill -9 <the 12 clients>   (all of them disconnect at the same moment)
  $ ps -o pid,ppid,stat,rss,cmd --ppid 18809
        PID    PPID STAT   RSS CMD
      18823   18809 Z+       0 [server] <defunct>
      18824   18809 Z+       0 [server] <defunct>
      18825   18809 Z+       0 [server] <defunct>
      18826   18809 Z+       0 [server] <defunct>
      18827   18809 Z+       0 [server] <defunct>
      18829   18809 Z+       0 [server] <defunct>
      18830   18809 Z+       0 [server] <defunct>
      18831   18809 Z+       0 [server] <defunct>
      18832   18809 Z+       0 [server] <defunct>
      18833   18809 Z+       0 [server] <defunct>
  children reaped: 2 of 12, zombies (STAT Z): 10
  the parent still counts active=10: it thinks those clients are connected
  server log:
    | 00:43:03.912 [server:18809] INFO  reaped child 18828: exit 3 (client left) | active=11
    | 00:43:03.919 [server:18809] INFO  reaped child 18822: exit 3 (client left) | active=10

--- [1] WITH: ./server -p 9090  ---
  $ ./client -p 9090 --mode idle   x 12 (connect, send nothing)
  12 children are serving them
  $ kill -9 <the 12 clients>   (all of them disconnect at the same moment)
  $ ps -o pid,ppid,stat,rss,cmd --ppid 18835
        PID    PPID STAT   RSS CMD
  children reaped: 12 of 12, zombies (STAT Z): 0
  server log:
    | 00:43:04.502 [server:18835] INFO  reaped child 18849: exit 3 (client left) | active=11
    | 00:43:04.508 [server:18835] INFO  reaped child 18848: exit 3 (client left) | active=10
    | ... and 10 more line(s) like these
  [PASS] [1] without (one waitpid per signal): 2 of 12 reaped, 10 stay zombies
  [PASS] [1] with the loop: all 12 reaped, 0 zombies

==== [2a] client leaves: SIGPIPE ignored, EPIPE handled ====

--- [2a] WITHOUT: ./server -p 9090 --no-sigpipe ---
  $ ./client -p 9090 --mode abort
    OK seq=1 pid=18863 host=LAPTOP-0F0NVT4H up=0d 22:03:47 load=0.00/0.04/0.00 mem_avail=7.05/7.61 GiB procs=224
    RESULT: got snapshot 1 of 10, closing the connection now
  next ./client after that: exit 0 (the parent keeps serving)
  server log:
    | 00:43:05.074 [server:18863] INFO  127.0.0.1:52448: WATCH 10 200 -> 10 snapshot(s)
    | 00:43:05.476 [server:18861] WARN  reaped child 18863: killed by signal 13 (Broken pipe) | active=0
    | 00:43:06.087 [server:18861] INFO  reaped child 18865: exit 0 (request served) | active=0

--- [2a] WITH: ./server -p 9090  ---
  $ ./client -p 9090 --mode abort
    OK seq=1 pid=18868 host=LAPTOP-0F0NVT4H up=0d 22:03:48 load=0.00/0.04/0.00 mem_avail=7.06/7.61 GiB procs=224
    RESULT: got snapshot 1 of 10, closing the connection now
  next ./client after that: exit 0 (the parent keeps serving)
  server log:
    | 00:43:06.357 [server:18868] INFO  127.0.0.1:52464: WATCH 10 200 -> 10 snapshot(s)
    | 00:43:06.759 [server:18868] INFO  127.0.0.1:52464: client left before snapshot 3/10 (Broken pipe) -> stop
    | 00:43:06.760 [server:18866] INFO  reaped child 18868: exit 3 (client left) | active=0
    | 00:43:07.369 [server:18866] INFO  reaped child 18870: exit 0 (request served) | active=0
  [PASS] [2a] without: the child is killed by SIGPIPE (signal 13)
  [PASS] [2a] with: write() returns EPIPE, the child logs it and exits 3
  [PASS] [2a] both: the next client is served

==== [2b] network vanishes: TCP_USER_TIMEOUT ====

--- [2b] WITHOUT: ./server -p 9090 --no-user-timeout ---
  $ ./client -p 9090 -n 20 -w 500   (20 snapshots in 10 s)
  after 2 snapshots the client's network vanishes, and so does the client:
  $ tc qdisc add dev lo root netem loss 100%   (drop every packet)
  $ kill -9 18872
  the child ended 9.0 s after the cut; the client had received 2 of 20
  server log:
    | 00:43:07.641 [server:18873] INFO  127.0.0.1:52486: WATCH 20 500 -> 20 snapshot(s)
    | 00:43:17.148 [server:18871] INFO  reaped child 18873: exit 0 (request served) | active=0

--- [2b] WITH: ./server -p 9090  ---
  $ ./client -p 9090 -n 20 -w 500   (20 snapshots in 10 s)
  after 2 snapshots the client's network vanishes, and so does the client:
  $ tc qdisc add dev lo root netem loss 100%   (drop every packet)
  $ kill -9 18877
  the child ended 4.0 s after the cut; the client had received 2 of 20
  server log:
    | 00:43:17.246 [server:18878] INFO  127.0.0.1:33048: WATCH 20 500 -> 20 snapshot(s)
    | 00:43:21.751 [server:18878] WARN  127.0.0.1:33048: client unreachable, no ACK for 3000 ms (Connection timed out) -> stop before snapshot 10/20
    | 00:43:21.752 [server:18876] INFO  reaped child 18878: exit 3 (client left) | active=0
  [PASS] [2b] without: every write() succeeds for 9.0 s, the child logs "request served" (client got 2 of 20)
  [PASS] [2b] with: write() fails with ETIMEDOUT 4.0 s after the cut, the child stops

==== [3] request validation: four malicious requests ====

--- [3] WITHOUT: ./server -p 9090 --no-validate ---
  (a) $ ./client -p 9090 --mode longline   (16 MiB, no newline)
      after 1.5 s the child is still reading: RSS 17844 KiB
      RESULT: sent all 16 MiB without a newline, waiting for the server
  (b) $ ./client -p 9090 -r "WATCH 4294967297 100"   (2^32 + 1)
      OK seq=1 pid=18885 host=LAPTOP-0F0NVT4H up=0d 22:04:05 load=0.00/0.04/0.00 mem_avail=7.08/7.61 GiB procs=218
  (c) $ ./client -p 9090 -r "WATCH 100 0"   (no pause between snapshots)
      100 snapshots in 22 ms
  (d) $ ./client -p 9090 -r "WATCH 100000 1000"   (one snapshot a second)
      after 1.5 s: 2 snapshot(s), the child keeps going: 100000 x 1 s = 27.8 hours
  server log:
    | 00:43:21.853 [server:18883] WARN  no newline after 8388607 bytes: request buffer grown to 16384 KiB
    | 00:43:21.858 [server:18883] WARN  no newline after 16775043 bytes: request buffer grown to 32768 KiB
    | 00:43:23.346 [server:18885] INFO  127.0.0.1:60048: WATCH 4294967297 100 -> 1 snapshot(s)
    | 00:43:23.357 [server:18887] INFO  127.0.0.1:60062: WATCH 100 0 -> 100 snapshot(s)
    | 00:43:23.374 [server:18889] INFO  127.0.0.1:60074: WATCH 100000 1000 -> 100000 snapshot(s)

--- [3] WITH: ./server -p 9090  ---
  (a) $ ./client -p 9090 --mode longline   (16 MiB, no newline)
      RESULT: server reply after 0.0 s: ERROR request too long
  (b) $ ./client -p 9090 -r "WATCH 4294967297 100"   (2^32 + 1)
      ERROR bad arguments: WATCH <count 1-100> <ms 100-10000>
  (c) $ ./client -p 9090 -r "WATCH 100 0"   (no pause between snapshots)
      ERROR bad arguments: WATCH <count 1-100> <ms 100-10000>
  (d) $ ./client -p 9090 -r "WATCH 100000 1000"   (one snapshot a second)
      ERROR bad arguments: WATCH <count 1-100> <ms 100-10000>
  server log:
    | 00:43:25.237 [server:18892] WARN  127.0.0.1:60080: request longer than 127 bytes -> rejected
    | 00:43:26.737 [server:18894] WARN  127.0.0.1:60086: bad WATCH arguments "WATCH 4294967297 100" -> rejected
    | 00:43:26.743 [server:18896] WARN  127.0.0.1:60102: bad WATCH arguments "WATCH 100 0" -> rejected
    | 00:43:26.749 [server:18898] WARN  127.0.0.1:60106: bad WATCH arguments "WATCH 100000 1000" -> rejected
  [PASS] [3] without (a): 16 MiB with no newline is buffered, child RSS 17844 KiB
  [PASS] [3] without (b): WATCH 4294967297 100 is served as WATCH 1 100
  [PASS] [3] without (c): WATCH 100 0 sends 100 snapshots in 22 ms
  [PASS] [3] without (d): WATCH 100000 1000 keeps a child busy for 27.8 hours
  [PASS] [3] with: all 4 requests rejected with an ERROR line

==== [4] request deadline: Slowloris ====

--- [4] WITHOUT: ./server -p 9090 --no-deadline ---
  $ ./client -p 9090 --mode slow   x 32 (1 byte every 0.5 s, never a newline)
  32 children, each waiting for a request line (server limit -m 32)
  4 s later: 32 children still waiting
  $ ./client -p 9090   (an ordinary client arrives)
    ERROR server busy, try again later
  slow clients that got "ERROR request timeout": 0
  server log:
    | 00:43:32.609 [server:18899] WARN  127.0.0.1:34610 rejected: 32 clients connected, limit 32

--- [4] WITH: ./server -p 9090  ---
  $ ./client -p 9090 --mode slow   x 32 (1 byte every 0.5 s, never a newline)
  32 children, each waiting for a request line (server limit -m 32)
  4 s later: 0 children still waiting
  $ ./client -p 9090   (an ordinary client arrives)
    OK seq=1 pid=19031 host=LAPTOP-0F0NVT4H up=0d 22:04:19 load=0.00/0.04/0.00 mem_avail=7.08/7.61 GiB procs=253
  slow clients that got "ERROR request timeout": 32
    RESULT: after 3.0 s and 7 bytes the server replied: ERROR request timeout
  server log:
    | 00:43:35.695 [server:18998] WARN  127.0.0.1:34616: no complete request line within 3000 ms (got "SYSINF") -> rejected
    | 00:43:35.698 [server:18999] WARN  127.0.0.1:34618: no complete request line within 3000 ms (got "SYSINFO") -> rejected
    | 00:43:35.699 [server:19000] WARN  127.0.0.1:34628: no complete request line within 3000 ms (got "SYSINFO") -> rejected
    | ... and 29 more line(s) like these
  [PASS] [4] without: 32 slow clients hold all 32 children, the next client is told busy
  [PASS] [4] with: all 32 cut off after 3 s, the next client is served

==== [5a] parent killed: children die with it (PR_SET_PDEATHSIG) ====

--- [5a] WITHOUT: ./server -p 9090 --no-pdeathsig ---
  $ ./client -p 9090 -n 10 -w 300   (10 snapshots in 3 s)
  $ ps -o pid,ppid,stat,rss,cmd --ppid 19032
        PID    PPID STAT   RSS CMD
      19034   19032 S+    1800 ./server -p 9090 --no-pdeathsig
  $ kill -9 19032   (the parent server crashes)
  child 19034 still running: STAT S, PPID 18765 (was 19032) -> orphan
  the client received 10 of 10 snapshots

--- [5a] WITH: ./server -p 9090  ---
  $ ./client -p 9090 -n 10 -w 300   (10 snapshots in 3 s)
  $ ps -o pid,ppid,stat,rss,cmd --ppid 19036
        PID    PPID STAT   RSS CMD
      19038   19036 S+    1824 ./server -p 9090
  $ kill -9 19036   (the parent server crashes)
  child 19038 is gone: the kernel sent it SIGTERM when the parent died
  the client received 3 of 10 snapshots
    00:43:40.317 [client:19037] WARN  after 3 reply line(s): the server closed the connection
  [PASS] [5a] without: the child outlives the parent as an orphan and sends all 10
  [PASS] [5a] with: the child ends with the parent (3 of 10 sent)

==== [5b] Ctrl+C: graceful shutdown ====

--- [5b] WITHOUT: ./server -p 9090 --no-graceful ---
  $ ./client -p 9090 -n 10 -w 300   (10 snapshots in 3 s)
  $ kill -INT -19040   (Ctrl+C: SIGINT to the server's whole process group)
  $ ./client -p 9090   (a new client, 0.2 s after Ctrl+C)
    00:43:41.679 [client:19043] ERROR cannot connect to 127.0.0.1:9090: Connection refused
  the running client received 3 of 10 snapshots
    00:43:41.470 [client:19041] WARN  after 3 reply line(s): the server closed the connection
  server: killed by signal 2 (Interrupt), 0.2 s after Ctrl+C
  server log:
    | 00:43:40.628 [server:19040] INFO  robustness: [4] request deadline ON | [5a] pdeathsig ON | [5b] graceful Ctrl+C OFF

--- [5b] WITH: ./server -p 9090  ---
  $ ./client -p 9090 -n 10 -w 300   (10 snapshots in 3 s)
  $ kill -INT -19044   (Ctrl+C: SIGINT to the server's whole process group)
  $ ./client -p 9090   (a new client, 0.2 s after Ctrl+C)
    00:43:42.741 [client:19047] ERROR cannot connect to 127.0.0.1:9090: Connection refused
  the running client received 10 of 10 snapshots
  server: exit 0, 1.9 s after Ctrl+C
  server log:
    | 00:43:41.692 [server:19044] INFO  robustness: [4] request deadline ON | [5a] pdeathsig ON | [5b] graceful Ctrl+C ON
    | 00:43:42.536 [server:19044] INFO  Ctrl+C: no new clients; waiting for 1 child(ren) to finish (at most 30 s, Ctrl+C again to quit now)
    | 00:43:44.446 [server:19044] INFO  reaped child 19046: exit 0 (request served) | active=0
    | 00:43:44.447 [server:19044] INFO  all children finished -> server exits
  [PASS] [5b] without: Ctrl+C kills the server and the child at once (3 of 10 sent)
  [PASS] [5b] with: new clients refused, the running one gets all 10, then exit 0

